From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 07:46:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(llama-cpp): the encoder outputs of an encoder-decoder
 model live on the device

On top of patches/0006 (the encoder output per sequence): the store is one
F32 tensor in its own backend buffer, written by the encoder graph
(ggml_set_rows) into the region the encode's memory context assigns and
committed after the compute, read by the decoder graph (ggml_get_rows).
No host copies of the encoder output remain; sequence operations move no
data; state writes carry the rows through the tensor path. No public API
changes; only T5 reaches the new code. Carried as a llama.cpp patch beside
the others (patches/0007-encoder-decoder-store.patch).

Checked on the CPU with a random-weight T5: the 0005 library tests, the
store unit test rewritten for the device store, and the 0004 server checks.

Assisted-by: Claude Code
